statement:
Let $A \subseteq \mathrm{Fin}\,n$ be a finite set of indices and let $g : \mathrm{Fin}\,n \to \bbr$. Then
\[
  \prod_{j \in A} g(j) \;=\; \prod_{j : \mathrm{Fin}\,n}
    \begin{cases} g(j) & \text{if } j \in A, \\ 1 & \text{if } j \notin A, \end{cases}
\]
so that a product taken only over the members of $A$ may equivalently be written as a product over all of $\mathrm{Fin}\,n$ in which each factor outside $A$ is replaced by $1$.
